.TH PALETTE 1
.SH NAME
palette \- the sixteen colours are not fixed
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/palette
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Palette
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/Palette.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
Sixteen swatches, each labelled with its colour name on its own
background.  A key rewrites every palette entry to a grey ramp and the
same swatches come back grey \- still naming BLUE and RED \- because a
colour index means whatever the palette says it means.  A second key sets
white alone back, and a third restores the rest.
.PP
This is a hardware palette register in the original.  Inferno resolves a
colour when the image is made, so the port keeps the palette in an array
and repaints from it: the same thing happens to the same drawing, but it
does not reach across the display.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B "any key"
Advance a stage; the last exits
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/palette.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
